------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT S IS, AND WHY THE HIGH END IS THE INTERESTING END
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  mass_bound (prereg, locked, exact):  |cell(r,d)| <= S(r,d),
  S(r,d) = sum_k C(d,k) N(r-k), the unsigned prime stencil mass.
  S is therefore the amount of prime mass the alternating sum had
  to annihilate to land on zero.  O46 found the median S at a
  resolved zero is 8-516 against a stratum median of 1e8-1e18, so
  the typical zero is a cell with almost nothing to cancel.  The
  high-S zeros are the ones where a large mass cancelled exactly.

